From: Kiln Project <kiln@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:08:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: tlv320aic31xx: fix swallowed reset failure on power-on

aic31xx_power_on() logs an error if aic31xx_reset() fails but then
falls through into regcache_sync() anyway, which overwrites `ret`.
A reset failure is therefore never actually reported to the caller,
the regulators are never disabled, and the regmap cache is never put
back into cache-only mode -- the device is left in a half-initialized
state that the rest of the driver assumes is fully reset.

Mirror the cleanup already done a few lines below for a
regcache_sync() failure: put the regmap back into cache-only mode,
disable the bulk regulators, and propagate the real error code.

Found while integrating this codec into a custom infotainment audio
stack and tracing a power-on retry that silently kept using a
half-reset device after an injected I2C NACK on the reset write.

Signed-off-by: Kiln Project <kiln@example.invalid>
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/tlv320aic31xx.c b/sound/soc/codecs/tlv320aic31xx.c
index e0a8db4..4763033 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tlv320aic31xx.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tlv320aic31xx.c
@@ -1281,8 +1281,13 @@ static int aic31xx_power_on(struct snd_soc_component *component)
 
 	/* Reset device registers for a consistent power-on like state */
 	ret = aic31xx_reset(aic31xx);
-	if (ret < 0)
+	if (ret < 0) {
 		dev_err(aic31xx->dev, "Could not reset device: %d\n", ret);
+		regcache_cache_only(aic31xx->regmap, true);
+		regulator_bulk_disable(ARRAY_SIZE(aic31xx->supplies),
+				       aic31xx->supplies);
+		return ret;
+	}
 
 	ret = regcache_sync(aic31xx->regmap);
 	if (ret) {
